WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"The Meg" -- you
have described the movie as --

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:04.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
like "Jurassic Park"
meets "Jaws."

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-This is a big shark.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.474 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-This is a giant shark.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:11.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
We set out to make the
second best shark movie ever.

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I think
we have achieved that.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's great.
-Yeah.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You got to know
what you're aiming for.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:19.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. We tried to take out
"Deep Blue Sea."

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, interesting.
-You know what I mean?

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:22.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
Little --
Little known shark reference.

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Little known. So you...
-Yeah.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.526
-You -- Obviously, a CGI shark.
-Yes.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.062
-You couldn't get any sharks
to agree to be in this movie.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
But --
-They wouldn't do it, yeah.

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:32.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But the real -- no CGI --
the real Jason Statham.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.835
You -- First time Wilson
and Statham have teamed up.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:38.238
-[ As Jason Statham ] "Oh, yeah.
First time with Statham."

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"That's right."

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:41.741
-I'd -- See, I would like
to be around Jason Statham.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it -- Is it as exciting
as it sounds?

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:46.546 size:78% position:39%
-I am like a fan girl
around Jason Statham.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I love his movies.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:50.150 size:84% position:42%
He is one of the few
action stars of like --

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he says, like,
"I'm going to kick your ass,"

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, you believe him.
-Yeah.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:55.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know?
-Yeah.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.991 size:88% position:44%
-He could kick the crap
out of people, you know?

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I believe that,
after takes of his movies,

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone's ass
had actually been kicked.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:03.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:04.531 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, absolutely.

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:07.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
But someone asked me in a --
in a press tour earlier,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:07.867 size:84% position:42% line:92%
they were saying, like,

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, if you were going to
voice The Meg,

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
if it was an animated --

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.006 line:92%
like, who should voice The Meg?"

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:15.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Well, Jason Statham."

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.142 line:92%
-[ Laughing ] Right, yeah.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that would be
an interesting conversation.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.846 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was be like...

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:23.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm going to make you bleed,
Jack."

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the shark
would be like,

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Not if I bite you
in half first."

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.422 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:32.992 line:92%
"I'd like to see you try."

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:36.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm going to swim to you
and bite you with my teeth."

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, whatever.
-Right.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.699 size:81% position:41%
-You know? You know?
-The sharks are, like,

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:42.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
historically bad at comebacks,
yeah.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.970 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The shark...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:46.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sharks...
-Yeah.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sharks like to write
their own material, you know.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.543
-Yeah, they're like, "I want to
just find it on the day."

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, just --
Yeah, improvise their lines.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.681 line:92%
-Are you afraid of sharks?

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:57.917
-I am -- I am afraid of sharks.
-Yeah.

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:01.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am also afraid of salmon.
-Okay, right.

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:01.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:05.425
I'm afraid of anything you're
going to find in the water...

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.192 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...that might swim
somewhat near you.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:10.797
-Yeah.
-So if it's a guppy or a minnow

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.500 size:78% position:39%
or a barnacle or a --
or a piece of kelp

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
that touches my calf,
I'm like -- I'm like, "Gaaah!"

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So I get out of the water.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:21.975
So am I afraid of sharks?
Yes, I am also afraid of sharks.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:22.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, see...
-So...

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.377
-But, like, that's not --
like, it's gonna be like --

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's just this one thing...
-Right.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...that Rainn's afraid of --
it's not that.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:30.183
-No, it's anything in the water
that touches my body

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
other than
sand and water itself.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:35.088
-And -- And a girl in a bikini.
Other than that...

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:38.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But -- But you -- you think
getting eaten by a shark,

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:41.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you had to go,
would be a cooler way to go.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It would be
an awesome way to go.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.364 line:92%
I mean, think about it --

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:47.500
like, the guy who played Dwight
was eaten by a shark?

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
It'd be like...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's badass!
-Yeah.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.373
-Am I right?
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:57.877
'Cause I -- there are
so many humiliating ways to die.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had one of those
in my life once.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
I borrowed
my handyman Pablo's van

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.517 line:92%
to go down to Home Depot once.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:05.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a true --
absolutely true story.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:08.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was
a 1974 Dodge huge van.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was --
I pulled it out in traffic.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I noticed the seat
was too far back,

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:15.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I kind of adjusted the bar
and slid it up.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:18.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then my --
it slid over my finger

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:19.899 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and my finger was stuck.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:23.369
And I could barely see
above the steering wheel.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.037 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I'm in traffic.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:26.406
And I'm like, "Aaah! Aaah! Aah!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm -- I'm --
And I can't find the brake.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:32.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm going down
Van Nuys Boulevard like this.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:35.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I -- And I really thought
in my head, like,

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:36.282 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"I'm going to die.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:40.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna die with my finger
under my anus."

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:40.987 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:44.357 size:81% position:41%
And...they're gonna --
they're gonna see me,

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:47.293
and, like, TMZ is going to take
photos of my body,

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is how
I will be found dead, like...

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:50.330 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:54.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I would absolutely love
to be eaten by a shark.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.803
-Yeah.
I hadn't thought of it that way.

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that -- yeah.
-Think about it.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.272
-People -- I'd be reading that,
being like,

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I would have thought he would
have had a newer van."

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:02.809 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Meg" --
I did not know this.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Meg"
is short for "Megalodon."

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:07.347 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-The megalodon, yes.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:09.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this is something
your son knew.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:12.285
-Yes, it -- it actually existed
like 100 million years ago.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:16.456
It was the biggest apex predator
that planet Earth has ever seen,

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:18.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
next to Jason Statham.
-Uh-huh.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:18.625 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:21.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my son was a huge fan
of megalodons.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:25.331
And he -- my mom actually
sent him a megalodon tooth.

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:25.765 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know
where she found it -- eBay?

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.836
I don't know where you get
a megalodon tooth, but --

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How big is a megalodon tooth?
-It's like this --

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's like this big.
-Okay.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:36.276
-It's like a big --
It's like a big, bony triangle.

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:37.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-And it's sharp.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my son
would come home from school.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he'd have an apple
for a snack.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:41.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he'd use it as a knife.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he would -- he'd be
cutting up slices of apple

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:47.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a -- with
a 100 million-year-old tooth.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:52.625
And that's the crazy life
that TV celebrities live.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.861
-Yeah, exactly.
-Now it's just weird, you know?

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:56.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just weird.
-"This is my son.

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:57.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
He cuts his meat
with a megalodon tooth."

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:58.498 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.498 --> 00:05:02.101
You play a -- but you actually
play an eccentric billionaire --

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...in this film.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.404 line:92%
And you have -- in real life,

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:06.172 size:75% position:38%
you've crossed paths
with billionaires.

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:09.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's an odd thing
that TV actors --

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:10.310 line:92%
billionaires love to hang out

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
with, like, sports figures
and, like, TV actors.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-And I've been at --

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
just at different events
and award shows and parties.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:18.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's billion --
chockablock with billionaires.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:19.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like,
"Oh, there's Elon Musk.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's other billionaires
and stuff."

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so
I really based this guy --

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's -- Jack Morris is --
he's kind of the comic relief

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, also, kind of the villain
in the movie.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:29.462 size:81% position:41%
So it's an interesting
kind of combination.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:31.831
But I took
some of those qualities that --

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
that billionaires have --
that, oftentimes,

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:37.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
billionaires have this kind of
like boyish sense of wonder

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:37.670 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
about the world.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:38.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you'll meet them,
and they're --

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:41.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're, like, in Air Jordans
and, like, a track suit.

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:43.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're like, "Hey, wow.
That's cool.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do these cameras work?
Whoa!"

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You know?

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:47.547 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They -- They --

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:49.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that kind of curiosity,
I think,

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
makes them who they are.
-Yeah.

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:53.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But they can also turn
real quick

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:54.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you see a dark side,
you know,

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:58.157
where they -- you know how they
got to where they got, you know?

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] Right, yeah.
-So...

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:00.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right,
the Air Jordans came later,

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:04.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the crazy genius part
was first.

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:05.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:07.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The evil Scrooge
capitalist genius

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:10.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
is underneath
that boyish wonder.

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:12.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's nice
to see that in film,

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:13.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's always wonderful
to see you here.

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:15.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for coming back.

